---
import { runFor, shownSeconds } from "../../../lib/benchmarks";
import Speed from "../speed.astro";

// Oxlint against the ESLint toolchain; Biome is compared on /providers.
const small = runFor(42);
const large = runFor(420);
const speedup = Math.round(large.ms.eslint / large.ms.oxlint);

// Differences of the rounded times shown, so the figures add up on the page.
const oxlintGrowth = Math.round(large.ms.oxlint) - Math.round(small.ms.oxlint);

const eslintGrowth = (
  shownSeconds(large.ms.eslint) - shownSeconds(small.ms.eslint)
).toFixed(1);
---

<Speed
  highlight="oxlint"
  id="ox-speed"
  stats={[
    {
      label: "Faster than the ESLint toolchain on 420 files",
      value: `${speedup}×`,
    },
    {
      label: "Added on Oxlint going from 42 to 420 files",
      unit: "ms",
      value: `+${oxlintGrowth}`,
    },
    {
      label: "Added on ESLint for the same growth",
      unit: "s",
      value: `+${eslintGrowth}`,
    },
  ]}
  title={`Ten times the files, ${oxlintGrowth} more milliseconds`}
  toolchains={["oxlint", "eslint"]}
>
  Oxlint and Oxfmt are native binaries that spread the work across every
  core, so a bigger project barely moves the clock. The ESLint toolchain runs
  in Node and slows down with every file you add.
  <Fragment slot="caption">
    <a class="underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-foreground" href="/providers"
      >How Biome compares</a
    >.
  </Fragment>
</Speed>
